# Append-only files: take both sides instead of asking a human.
#
# A changelog entry and an ADR are added at the same place by every branch that
# has one, so two branches in flight always collide there, and the resolution is
# always the same: keep both. `merge=union` does that, and it is safe here
# precisely because nothing in these files depends on anything else in them.
#
# Deliberately not applied to any .nix file. Union merge on code produces
# something that parses and means the wrong thing, which is worse than a
# conflict.
CHANGELOG.md    merge=union
architecture.md merge=union
